 "about": "Beech with silver fir and sycamore on the slopes, Norway spruce higher up and in the cold hollows; hop hornbeam, manna ash and downy oak on warm limestone, sessile and Turkey oak with hornbeam and ash in the low valleys; black and Scots pine on dolomite and canyon walls, Bosnian pine and mountain pine at the treeline; hazel, hawthorn and juniper on the pastures, dwarf juniper above the trees; rush-leaved moor-grass on the high karst pastures, alpine flowers, bilberry, ferns and bracken; flocks of sheep, Simmental cattle, horses and goats; plastered and stone houses. Hawthorn stands in for the plum orchards.",
